xnu 0304: the battery, published off the frame path

The status bar lost the battery when the old code was dropped: an SPMI VADC
read on the PMK8350 (PPID 0x31, channel 0x8f vbat_sns, divider 3) and an
IOPMPowerSource that turns one sample into a percentage from the 20-point
curve, a capacity out of the 5160 mAh pack and the properties iOS 16 reads
(AppleRawCurrentCapacity, the legacy IOBatteryInfo dictionary, updateStatus).

The old kernel ran both inside AppleCLCD::vsyncFired, on every 120th tick --
every 2 s, on the thread that presents frames, where a worst-case ADC read is
about 100 ms of polling, i.e. six dropped frames. The cadence here is a thread
of its own, started by mondrian_spmi_probe(): it sleeps 2 s, reads vbat and
vbus and calls MondrianPowerSource::updateState() through
mondrian_battery_publish(). Nothing in this patch touches swap(), present(),
vsyncFired() or the vsync timer.

A sample outside 3000-4400 mV is dropped before it can reach the status bar,
and a repeated identical sample publishes and logs nothing. The power source
is created lazily and attaches to the display, the parent the old kernel gave
it, so a sample that arrives before AppleCLCD is registered publishes nothing
and the next one retries. "sa [SID [CHAN [DIV]]]" on the USB control channel
runs one conversion by hand and answers with the ring's old line, e.g.
"sa sid 3 chan 0x08f div 3 = 4108 mV".

FullyCharged mirrors external power and IsCharging is false, as before: there
is no charger driver and the charger is behind the ADSP
(docs/MONDIAN_POWER.md). Temperature is the constant 2500 and capacity is
derived from the sample, not integrated.

